Trade goods, or Commodities in Elite, are produced and consumed by any of the dozen or so economies. Even if there are far more kinds of constructions, you have 5 options in constructing your Primary Port.

Note: Economies are listed in this section to help you pick systems. Explanations about how to put them to more use will be in the next section
Available Primary Port Economies:

Colony Economy:
Adaptable, easily changes and morphs into almost any other economy depending on where it is placed
Static Economies:
Durable, compared to Colony Economies, and require work to change
High Tech
Industrial
Military
Service/Pirate Economy:
Unique in that it helps enable Black Markets in stations that have Strong Service links, and will sell illicit goods. Can be inherited by larger stations that are built in the same orbit.
Water World (WW)/Earth-Like World (ELW) Population Dividend: 

The first (and only the first) Station that is built over a WW/ELW gets a massive population bonus. It is recommended to try to avoid building anything less than a Tier 2, but preferably a Tier 3 to snag this bonus.
Economy Overrides:

If you are building a Colony Economy, WHERE the Primary Port is going to be built is important. We will go into economy selection/building in more detail in the next section, but generally if any of these are present on or around the body you’re building on, they will change Colony economies and heavily influence other economies. It is generally not a good idea to fight the Overrides if at all possible.
